# Testing and quality

- Every behavior change includes direct tests; every fix includes a regression test.
- Structure tests as Arrange-Act-Assert or Given-When-Then with deterministic names and data.
- Target at least 95% line/statement coverage for new or materially changed
  executable production code where coverage tooling exists.
- Preserve current repository and CI gates; report actual thresholds, results, and gaps instead
  of claiming that this rule enforces coverage.
- Test success, validation, authorization, tenant isolation, error, timeout, cancellation,
  retry, idempotency, and safe fallback behavior as applicable.
- Declarative assets use build-failing behavior matrices, not source-line percentages.
